import VOPM.CoinedWalk

/-!
# Published E₈ root coordinates as input data (scaled by two)

Standard E₈ roots are the 112 integer roots with two coordinates ±1 and
the 128 half-integer roots with entries ±1/2 and an even count of minus signs.

We store **twice** those known roots, so every coordinate is an integer:
112 vectors with two entries ±2, 128 vectors with eight entries ±1.

This file **encodes published data**, not a new theorem classifying E₈.
The 8D periodic torus is currently an auxiliary graph, not a construction
of the exact E₈ lattice quotient. Different roots may alias modulo small N.

The explicit array is deterministic. A vector of length 240 makes missing
or surplus entries a Lean type error.
-/

namespace VOPM.E8Data

